details.image_prompt:
[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. Two white matte ceramic bowls are positioned on a rustic, aged oak wooden table with visible grain and small crumbs. One bowl is in sharp focus in the foreground, the other slightly blurred behind it. The composition is a 3/4 overhead angle, showing every component inside the bowls. Each bowl contains a base of warm, slightly steamed brown rice. Resting side-by-side on top of the rice are succulent, pink-and-white thawed shrimp, crisp bright green chopped cucumber, vibrant orange matchstick carrots, and soft, creamy diced avocado. A creamy, pale orange spicy yogurt dressing is drizzled artfully across the ingredients, with a few small droplets on the rim of the bowl. The surface is topped with a scattering of toasted brown sesame seeds. Props include a small wooden spoon resting near the foreground bowl and a few scattered sesame seeds and a small piece of cucumber on the oak surface. Soft natural side light from a window to the left creates gentle shadows and highlights the texture of the shrimp and the moisture of the dressing. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene looks like a home-cooked lunch—warm, lived-in, and authentic. Slight natural imperfections like a small sauce drip and uneven ingredient placement. No plastic sheen, no artificial symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No text, no watermarks, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography."
  }
]
